From 327ae37e2961ca624551a0b244d67d96a3ee8bf4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dan on Selwyn <dan@awto.au>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:12:02 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Run on Amaranth 0.6: keep Record in-tree, copy
 lib.coding.Encoder, use public imports

Amaranth 0.6 removes amaranth.hdl.rec (Record), amaranth.lib.coding,
ValueCastable.lowermethod and the public amaranth.hdl.<submodule> modules.

- luna/gateware/utils/record.py: Amaranth 0.5.10's Record on public API only.
- luna/gateware/utils/coding.py: Encoder, as amaranth.lib.coding asks.
- Point every Record/DIR_* import at the new module; replace amaranth.hdl.xfrm
  and amaranth.hdl.ast imports with top-level ones.
- interface/jtag.py: ECP5DebugSPIBridge memoises as_value itself instead of
  ValueCastable.lowermethod, so the module imports on 0.6.

The 93 tests pass on Amaranth 0.5.10 and 0.6.0.dev140.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
